1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,287
Laddoo Lab now sells in ten local shops.

2
00:00:03,587 --> 00:00:06,688
Then one shopkeeper calls
Arjun, and he is angry.

3
00:00:07,238 --> 00:00:09,744
Your online shop is cheaper than my shop!

4
00:00:09,744 --> 00:00:11,925
How do you keep every seller happy?

5
00:00:12,575 --> 00:00:15,385
Last time, Laddoo Lab chose its channels.

6
00:00:15,735 --> 00:00:19,874
A channel is the path a product takes,
from the kitchen to the customer.

7
00:00:20,224 --> 00:00:22,599
Arjun delivers to ten local shops.

8
00:00:22,599 --> 00:00:25,395
A supermarket chain stocks the packs too.

9
00:00:25,745 --> 00:00:28,138
And Dev runs a small online shop.

10
00:00:28,138 --> 00:00:30,035
Three paths, one product.

11
00:00:30,685 --> 00:00:32,481
So what is channel management?

12
00:00:32,781 --> 00:00:37,376
Philip Kotler and Gary Armstrong
explain it in Principles of Marketing.

13
00:00:37,726 --> 00:00:42,078
It means selecting, managing and motivating
each channel member, and checking

14
00:00:42,078 --> 00:00:43,806
their performance over time.

15
00:00:44,156 --> 00:00:48,488
A channel member is any business that
helps sell your product, like a shop

16
00:00:48,488 --> 00:00:49,624
or a wholesaler.

17
00:00:49,974 --> 00:00:53,936
In simple words: pick good partners,
help them sell, and check how they

18
00:00:53,936 --> 00:00:54,836
do.

19
00:00:54,976 --> 00:00:56,315
Watch Arjun do it.

20
00:00:56,315 --> 00:00:58,290
First, he selects the shops.

21
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,093
He visits twelve shops near
schools, and checks three things.

22
00:01:02,443 --> 00:01:03,995
Do parents shop there?

23
00:01:03,995 --> 00:01:05,000
Is it clean?

24
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,512
Does it pay on time?

25
00:01:06,862 --> 00:01:08,054
Ten shops pass.

26
00:01:08,054 --> 00:01:09,295
Two are dropped.

27
00:01:09,945 --> 00:01:11,659
Next, he motivates them.

28
00:01:11,659 --> 00:01:14,225
Each shop earns a margin on every pack.

29
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:17,681
A margin is the part of
the price the shop keeps.

30
00:01:18,031 --> 00:01:22,986
Arjun also gives every shop a display
stand, and fresh packs every Monday.

31
00:01:23,636 --> 00:01:24,870
Then he evaluates.

32
00:01:24,870 --> 00:01:28,258
Every Saturday, he counts
the packs sold in each shop.

33
00:01:28,608 --> 00:01:30,177
Nine shops sell well.

34
00:01:30,177 --> 00:01:32,122
One shop sells only a few.

35
00:01:32,472 --> 00:01:33,372
Why?

36
00:01:32,969 --> 00:01:35,520
Its stand is hidden behind the counter.

37
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:38,064
Arjun moves the stand to the front.

38
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:39,932
The next week, sales go up.

39
00:01:40,582 --> 00:01:42,472
Your sellers are your partners.

40
00:01:42,472 --> 00:01:44,091
When they win, you win.

41
00:01:44,791 --> 00:01:46,968
Now, back to the angry shopkeeper.

42
00:01:46,968 --> 00:01:48,910
This is called channel conflict.

43
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:54,801
Channel conflict means channel members
disagree about goals, roles or rewards.

44
00:01:55,151 --> 00:01:59,838
Vertical conflict happens between
levels of the same channel, like a shop

45
00:01:59,838 --> 00:02:01,694
against Laddoo Lab itself.

46
00:02:02,044 --> 00:02:06,660
Horizontal conflict happens at the same
level, like one shop against another

47
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,560
shop.

48
00:02:07,563 --> 00:02:11,342
Here, the shop is fighting
Laddoo Lab's own online shop.

49
00:02:11,342 --> 00:02:12,762
So it is vertical.

50
00:02:13,112 --> 00:02:15,117
Zoya fixes it in two steps.

51
00:02:15,117 --> 00:02:17,152
First, one price everywhere.

52
00:02:17,502 --> 00:02:20,767
Second, online orders near
a shop go to that shop.

53
00:02:20,767 --> 00:02:23,389
The shop delivers, and keeps its margin.

54
00:02:24,039 --> 00:02:26,006
Where do we see this at work today?

55
00:02:26,356 --> 00:02:27,256
Selecting.

56
00:02:27,152 --> 00:02:31,200
A phone maker picks stores that
can show and repair its phones.

57
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:32,450
Motivating.

58
00:02:32,421 --> 00:02:36,008
A paint company gives its
dealers bonuses and training.

59
00:02:36,358 --> 00:02:37,258
Evaluating.

60
00:02:37,248 --> 00:02:41,222
A medicine company checks which
chemists reorder every month.

61
00:02:41,572 --> 00:02:42,914
Managing conflict.

62
00:02:42,914 --> 00:02:47,594
A car maker gives each dealer its
own area, so dealers don't clash.

63
00:02:48,244 --> 00:02:50,774
But is a bigger channel always better?

64
00:02:50,774 --> 00:02:51,679
Not always.

65
00:02:52,029 --> 00:02:53,083
The good side.

66
00:02:53,083 --> 00:02:56,777
Shops earn more, and families
find the packs close to home.

67
00:02:57,127 --> 00:02:58,297
The hard side.

68
00:02:58,297 --> 00:03:00,792
Every margin costs Laddoo Lab money.

69
00:03:00,792 --> 00:03:02,976
And big buyers have big power.

70
00:03:03,326 --> 00:03:07,012
The supermarket asks for
packs that last three months.

71
00:03:07,012 --> 00:03:08,153
Nani says no.

72
00:03:08,153 --> 00:03:09,442
No preservatives.

73
00:03:09,792 --> 00:03:13,177
So they agree on smaller,
fresher deliveries every week.

74
00:03:13,527 --> 00:03:16,623
Kotler also notes that
some conflict is healthy.

75
00:03:16,623 --> 00:03:18,809
It pushes everyone to do better.

76
00:03:19,159 --> 00:03:20,059
The lesson?

77
00:03:19,998 --> 00:03:24,257
Treat sellers as partners, but never
break your promise to the customer.

78
00:03:24,907 --> 00:03:25,830
Quick check.

79
00:03:25,830 --> 00:03:29,210
A local shop is angry that
the supermarket is cheaper.

80
00:03:29,210 --> 00:03:31,219
What kind of conflict is this?

81
00:03:33,119 --> 00:03:34,019
Horizontal!

82
00:03:33,934 --> 00:03:37,155
Both are shops, at the
same level of the channel.

83
00:03:37,755 --> 00:03:38,764
So, remember.

84
00:03:39,064 --> 00:03:43,844
Channel management means selecting,
motivating and evaluating your sellers.

85
00:03:44,194 --> 00:03:49,163
Conflict can be vertical, between
levels, or horizontal, at the same level.

86
00:03:49,513 --> 00:03:51,255
And treat sellers as partners.

87
00:03:51,255 --> 00:03:52,785
When they win, you win.

88
00:03:53,385 --> 00:03:58,380
Next time: one voice everywhere, with
integrated marketing communications.
